lusive reproduction requires renewed planning, not adjusted assertions.\n9. Complete independent whole-feature/source and companion assessment of every diff continuation. Historical captures, successful diagnostics and partial reviews certify no new content.\n\n## Delivery and completion\n\nRecheck head, base, request revision, provenance, authority and actual holds at every action boundary; revalidate if content or dev advances. Preserve inherited native/source-validation safeguards without deploying them or inventing an upstream PR prerequisite for PR #9.\n\nRetain genuine credential/security, owner-input/veto/cancel, operational and applicable exact-head protected gates. Do not alter frozen rollout bytes, repeat completed deployments or take over handed-off branches.\n\nThe coordinator must verify recommendation-policy companion completion, independent resolution records, safe activation and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices. Preserve authenticated Q/A, notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful exclusive lifecycle labels including `agent:writing`, and one 30-minute open-PR orchestrator with idle exit.\n\nPreserve dependency direction: #10 requires #9’s actual dev merge/ancestry; #37 retains its separate #39 dependency. Continue monitoring and aligned repairs until #9 and every qualifying companion/correction/repair PR successfully merge into `dev` and required post-merge validation completes. This correction alone does not complete that parent objective.\n"}],"producer_id":"local:e8dd20c11f5043518c59e21e41d4074c","questions":[{"answer_index":16,"id":"fbd480038ee660edb95dd3690683161a39480ffc41dfac01f8e147887794ef84","text":"Can the coordinator expose a fresh database-picker capture with its heading widget rows, compositor rows, exported SVG, and hash-bound final PNG through source_files evidence? The available layer evidence is historical, and its PNG is inaccessible. The reviewed plan requires identifying the first failing layer before changing picker presentation or capture/export."},{"answer_index":18,"id":"9a11147e3ffd85ce140c8f1244a1b15377efd00916e606a8b431a2d03a92488d","text":"The fresh receipt binds capture `38731476440` to candidate `3e6d6e980ea7f1e1c3a6412cb9c5cc824aa87df5` and the saved checkpoint. Widget rows, compositor rows and parsed SVG all retain the complete heading, including the `c`. This does not establish a production picker defect.\n\n1. **Coordinator tooling question:** Can `read_evidence_image` be exposed in this planner session for the supplied hash-bound PNG? It is absent from the available tools, and `read_image` returns “Source tool unavailable or invalid.” PNG inspection is still needed before specifying a presentation or export correction.\n\nNo owner decision or replacement upload is needed. Raw SVG bytes are not supplied. The publication transport repair also remains coordinator-owned; complete task history must be preserved."},{"answer_index":19,"id":"16d4d781180edfb004dda9a37d5c640ea072ea2cc5775a4681e92c27f584ab07","text":"Can the coordinator provide the reviewed plan’s GitHub reproduction with actual raw and framed SVG bytes, renderer versions, and available/selected font diagnostics, bound to the candidate, checkpoint and PNG hashes? PNG inspection now works and confirms the obscured `c`; terminal rows and parsed SVG preserve it. The supplied artifacts still cannot distinguish framing from rasterization, so a correction would be speculative."},{"answer_index":20,"id":"9d7dfd33ccfb0fff403dc64cf5154bb0084c6d340b3db71751df45304dbb3650","text":"Coordinator: please expose the exact pre-invocation checkpoint source for tests/agent_tools/render_diagnostics.py. I mistakenly treated a capped 300-line read as complete and omitted its remaining lines when writing. Restore that file’s original suffix before retaining my focused additions. Please also verify the restored README against the saved checkpoint. No owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":21,"id":"962ad2658075e133178b0c27a43c436c00ea5a63640a4a6e0dafbca91a41dc09","text":"Coordinator: please run the approved isolated GitHub candidate capture from the preserved checkpoint, including the restored diagnostic tests and existing SVG-evidence helper/tests. Expose hash-bound database-picker raw/framed SVG content, font/renderer diagnostics and PNG through source_files. The reviewed plan requires this evidence before selecting a heading correction; no owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":22,"id":"d82141d33b770fcc68e14949f0292959e0f2597aa4301b71d32ab7338f57b0e7","text":"1. The current logs prove checkbox text loss but do not identify its first failing layer; they also report coverage totals without exact missing arcs. Which correction sequence should the plan use?\nEvidence first (Recommended): Fix behavior-preserving Ruff/format issues, add bounded failing-state diagnostics and focused task-related regressions, and obtain exact-head GitHub reproduction plus coverage JSON before selecting a checkbox production repair.\nSeparate diagnostic checkpoint: Keep this step diagnostic-only; obtain checkbox state and coverage evidence on GitHub, then independently plan all lint, test and production corrections together."},{"answer_index":23,"id":"e896f2e46da935a3d8d2023d77a872fd7f6624fbdae4625988d391767b3be2a6","text":"I read the complete current-head check records and all failed-job log parts. Existing feature requirements remain settled; no new owner preference is needed. Three coordinator evidence questions remain before a concrete repair plan:\n\n1. **Picker correction:** Can the coordinator expose capture `38927473247`’s hash-bound receipt, database-picker geometry, complete raw/framed SVGs, and all four comparison PNGs? The visual evidence tools currently return “Source tool unavailable or invalid.” The reviewer’s framing finding needs direct inspection before selecting the export correction.\n\n2. **Coverage:** Can the coordinator expose canonical `coverage.json` from run `38927048857`, bound to head `e3246e88769588cf10b61b5d8de3de1193c43ba2`? Branch coverage is **98.02% against 98.03%**. Exact missing arcs are needed to specify meaningful task-related regressions without changing baselines.\n\n3. **Type-menu failure:** Can the coordinator provide a bounded GitHub reproduction capturing focus, `type_input`, matches, scroll offsets, field/viewport geometry, and queued layout state immediately before the failing initial `assert menu.display` on Python 3.13/3.14? This will distinguish fixture timing from a production positioning defect before choosing a repair.\n\nThese are coordinator artifact requests, not requests for owner uploads or approval. No files were changed and no programs were executed."},{"answer_index":24,"id":"b239df38a3cbbd33de3627b25a36e9063e036dac68b6e9c97c83d69c701c88f3","text":"1. The rejected PNG and widget/compositor rows show `SELECT c.c│FROM`: rendering replaces the existing separator space with a bar. Should the correction preserve every in-document whitespace cell using the thin underline fallback, reserving vertical bars for end-of-line and empty-line padding?\nPreserve whitespace (Recommended): Keep spaces and expanded tabs intact for primary and secondary carets; retain colors, cell widths and completion behavior, and add focused rendering and completion regressions."},{"answer_index":25,"id":"ba800d0ea428ec7a001c0765a90362402cdfe85aa29ac8ae5d7e49a96975ad4b","text":"1. Should the plan restore the newly pinned dev’s capture/export safeguards before completing the outstanding independent review? The current diff deletes `.github/agent/capture_artifact.py`, its regression module and a parent-objective record, reverts `agent-visual.yml`, and removes failed-capture documentation.\nPreserve dev safeguards (Recommended): Restore those files and workflow exactly from pinned dev, retain its documentation plus the feature-specific activation section, preserve the complete SQL Explorer patch, then obtain fresh review and GitHub validation.\nReview before reconciliation: Complete read-only assessment of the published predecessor first; keep current-base reconciliation and final candidate validation blocked until separately planned."},{"answer_index":26,"id":"7955d1db22074defa82b9d57196aac7ba36a0679d4226fe9ad241de670ff3d1e","text":"1. Should the renewed plan preserve the inherited column ruler and route the reported stray “1” for independent reassessment, using the inspected PNG, separate ruler/editor geometry, identical pinned-dev ruler source, and existing empty-document assertion? This resolves the correction approach only; the rejecting visual gate remains in force until independently reviewed.\nPreserve ruler (Recommended): Preserve production presentation; add a focused tab-switch ruler/gutter regression and explicit scene evidence, then repeat independent full-feature and visual review.\nChange ruler presentation: Authorize a narrow presentation change to distinguish column labels from gutter numbers; its exact appearance needs a further decision before implementation."},{"answer_index":27,"id":"46377a331dc01c2e34cff52b83d9ddd5e5dd1b98a41de0000d6832f0d20a0a45","text":"1. Should the renewed plan first collect bounded, GitHub-only evidence for the indistinct secondary carets before choosing a production or export repair? The inspected PNG confirms the visibility finding, but its geometry does not identify the failing layer.\nDiagnose first (Recommended): Preserve the complete feature and selected ruler work; add exact cursor/focus/scroll state, caret-cell widget/compositor styles and lossless SVG evidence with focused regressions, then independently plan the demonstrated repair after GitHub capture.\nChange caret presentation: Plan a production presentation change now; its precise appearance requires another choice and must preserve SQL, whitespace, colors, widths and mapping."},{"answer_index":28,"id":"1533c21a5bce25f66a9d4d6d9395969fe2d15e25112b4e9000ea13507588cdd7","text":"1. May the renewed plan include narrow repairs for the newly verified journal-error status and new-file dialog alignment, after identifying their failing layers? These extend the earlier enumerated UI repair scope.\nNarrow gate repairs (Recommended): Show read failures without claiming empty results, restore intended dialog centering, add focused regressions, and retain the complete feature and all review gates.\n\n2. Should the correction fix the confirmed diagnostic/test defects and collect missing command-caret and ruler lifecycle evidence before selecting further presentation or focus changes?\nFaithful diagnostics (Recommended): Fix variable shadowing and lint, preserve combining marks and cell styles during cropping, retain strict assertions, and diagnose ruler focus/width and command-caret layers on GitHub without forcing scene state."},{"answer_index":29,"id":"310ef79ccea7f258fef9f5fee47aebad16404f96b3ab0e5fc0e03fac1fad6e90","text":"1. Which correction sequence should the renewed plan specify for the observed ruler focus and row-width failures? Existing assertions and production ruler presentation must remain intact.\nTrace lifecycle (Recommended): Fix the confirmed lint/format findings, preserve current-dev safeguards, and add bounded GitHub-only callback-order and strip-padding observations before selecting the focus or width correction.\nCorrect scene lifecycle: Plan command focus after tab restoration and full-width widget-row collection now; retain strict equality and negative controls, then require GitHub reproduction and independent review."},{"answer_index":30,"id":"fd123ca6bb2e97c0179d0650913397f70c39425e6f71229ff3f98ad248a446a7","text":"1. Should the renewed plan correct the demonstrated harness-layer mismatch: apply the scene’s intended command focus after deferred tab restoration, and compare Textual’s styled widget rows with compositor rows while retaining the original unpadded strips as separate evidence? Production tab behavior and ruler presentation would stay unchanged; strict equality, negative controls, and all feature/review gates remain required.\nCorrect harness layers (Recommended): Use ordered scene initialization and native styled-row collection, preserve raw observations, fix confirmed lint/format findings, and validate on GitHub.\nExtend diagnostics first: Preserve the failing harness and collect native styled-row and focus-application traces on GitHub before separately planning its correction."},{"answer_index":31,"id":"4eabbb1c0750e4fc0765750745d410dec1b52cf5617089e9dfd9c6176b220bff","text":"1. Should the renewed correction replace the tab/database scene’s fixed 0.3-second switch timer with the existing workspace mount-completion hook, ordering database switching after workspace initialization and its deferred restoration, then applying command focus once? The Python 3.12 trace shows workspace completion arriving after scene initialization; preserve every strict ordering assertion, production tab behavior, and the complete feature.\nOrder mount completion (Recommended): Use the existing pending_mount_action hook and ordered scene continuations; add a deterministic delayed-mount regression, correct lint/format findings, and require independent review plus GitHub CI and all 46 visual scenes."},{"answer_index":32,"id":"659c61c7bd86b5bbc53d59c646f62f30d7371c88f1dafedfd973d6d8ac09aa59","text":"1. Should the renewed plan preserve the complete checkpoint and selected mount-ordering correction, fix the confirmed import/format findings, and obtain six GitHub-only caret raster comparisons before selecting an export repair? The latest coordinator report supplies a recommendation, not an approved implementation choice.\nSix comparisons (Recommended): For keyboard-multicursor and editor-command-caret, retain direct, actual 2× intermediate, and reduced PNGs under original declarations and a diagnostic-only verified DejaVu Sans Mono declaration; preserve production rendering, exact SVG/settings/font hashes, bounded lossless evidence, all assertions and review gates."},{"answer_index":33,"id":"706b7cb93eb62f050815bd403f89b787ee00056be012dbafa618eeda9492f614","text":"The feature choices are settled. Current-head run `39133140732` confirms import ordering, formatting, and a mount-ordering failure (`20 < 11`). The saved checkpoint already contains mount-hook work; those earlier failures cannot validate it.\n\nTwo coordinator questions remain before a complete plan can pass independent review. No owner preference or upload is needed.\n\n1. **Capture prerequisites:** Can the coordinator provide current, source-pinned evidence identifying the authorized isolated GitHub capture route, producer/consumer revisions, artifact compatibility, activation state, and applicable operational/protected holds? It must establish whether the selected twelve retained caret-stage PNGs and border diagnostics can be collected without modifying frozen deployments or overriding holds.\n\n2. **Prerequisite representation:** Can the coordinator resolve those external conditions and supply their evidence, or provide a separately reviewed supported mechanism for retaining them in the plan-review contract? The previous independent review rejected the plan because these conditions cannot be represented as `pr_dev_merge`. They must not be omitted or converted into fictitious PR dependencies.\n\nPR #10’s dependency on #9, and #37’s dependency on #39, remain downstream obligations—not prerequisites for #9.\n\nI’m stopping with these evidence questions rather than issuing another plan with unresolved consequential prerequisites. No files were edited or programs executed."},{"answer_index":34,"id":"1f4786be9b181443cf96946f2a96c395e841d6f855d3911ccf6a8fbdc95a336f","text":"1. Should the renewed plan preserve pinned dev 388b2eb’s capture-isolation/source-validation files, tests, evidence records and workflow safeguards, removing the saved patch’s stale reversions while retaining all SQL Explorer changes? This reconciles source only; actual deployed capture routing and protected approvals remain coordinator checks.\nPreserve current dev (Recommended): Restore inherited safeguards from immutable dev, retain feature-specific diagnostic additions, and require fresh independent review and GitHub validation.\nAssess reversions separately: Keep reconciliation blocked while the coordinator supplies a separately reviewed justification for each inherited safeguard removal.\n\n2. Should validation follow pinned dev’s Python 3.9–3.14 runtime matrix and Python 3.9 minimum environment, retaining public Python 3.8 metadata/static syntax compatibility? Earlier plans used Python 3.8 runtime environments, which the saved patch currently reinstates.\nPreserve dev matrix (Recommended): Remove stale Python 3.8 runtime-profile reversions, retain required Pillow test dependencies and coverage artifacts, and preserve public Python 3.8 compatibility.\nRetain Python 3.8 runs: Explicitly retain Python 3.8 runtime coverage in addition to dev’s Python 3.9 minimum environment, requiring reviewed compatibility configuration."},{"answer_index":35,"id":"643a4b634d7bcf859d32cb1ec804db30a977fb67e2b35d7e66f4af3c2951d3f0","text":"1. Should the correction complete the fake new-file screen in tests/agent_tools/visual_evidence.py with centered viewport/dialog geometry, resolved alignment and query_one support, preserving every required-element and stale-evidence assertion plus the real mounted centering regressions?\nComplete fixture (Recommended): Repair the six demonstrated fixture failures without bypassing alignment checks or changing production behavior.\n\n2. The inspected stage PNGs and diagnostics locate the command-caret visibility failure between intact SVG underline styling and raster output; neither tested font declaration resolves it. Should the renewed plan use an export-only explicit thin underline derived from actual underlined terminal spans, preserving text, colors, coordinates, clips and terminal behavior, with a real raster visibility regression and fresh full-scene review?\nFaithful export underlines (Recommended): Represent the existing underline as SVG geometry; retain original evidence, supersampling and all twelve stage comparisons, without introducing bars or blocks over text."}],"replacements":[],"source":"user","starting_prompt":"sql explorer: 1) if ctrl+shift+arrow up/down is pressed, then we should not spawn multiple cursors, instead selection should be expanded to the left until the line start, and next line until cursor's column (vs code like), it can be repeated multiple times to select many lines 2) now it seems that when multiple cursors is spawned, then I ctrl+c something and ctrl+v each cursor inserts WHOLE clipboard. instead each should have its own clipboard (VS code like)","task_id":"e8dd20c11f5043518c59e21e41d4074c","version":2}